From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: WinUI 2 pieces for Windows Terminal

Windows Terminal is a WinUI 2 application: its markup (and Microsoft.UI.Xaml's theme dictionaries) uses classes and members Windows.UI.Xaml did not have yet, and its window stayed hidden. This adds them: GridLength/CornerRadius/Thickness/Point/Rect/Size helpers, the IconSource family (FontIconSource, SymbolIconSource, BitmapIconSource, PathIconSource, IconSourceElement) and BitmapIcon, ToolTip objects as ToolTipService.ToolTip, AutomationProperties statics 2-8, Path and PathGeometry with the path markup language, DispatcherTimer, DurationHelper, XamlCompositionBrushBase and AcrylicBrush (drawn in their FallbackColor), Timeline statics, XamlLight and UIElement.Lights, FlyoutBase (composable, attached flyouts), AppBarToggleButton, MenuFlyoutItem3 and MenuFlyoutSubItem, ListViewItem's factory, ScrollBar, SwapChainPanel (it keeps the swap chain it is given; presenting it comes later), an iterable ResourceDictionary and PropertyChangedEventArgs. A hosted island raises Loading, Loaded and LayoutUpdated after its content is set even before it is painted, and its thread has a CoreDispatcher and a DispatcherQueue (DependencyObject.Dispatcher, Window.Dispatcher). Compiled markup: x:Load elements (a DeferredElement holding a section reference) are made when FindName asks for them and put in their place; an object written as a root inside the tree no longer ends the reading; an x:Name on an object without a Name member and classes that cannot be made no longer fail the whole file; read-only collection members of the application's types are added to; Silverlight's markup namespace is taken as the presentation one.
---
